	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Upload clipboard or Finder images to CloudFlare ImgBed.

Requires Alfred 5 Powerpack and Xcode Command Line Tools (/usr/bin/python3).

Setup
1. Open the workflow [x] panel
2. Set ImgBed URL (no trailing slash)
3. Set the user auth code from the ImgBed admin (not the admin password)
4. Channel defaults to cfr2; use telegram if R2 is not configured
5. Double-click the Hotkey object and assign a shortcut

Usage
• Select an image in Finder → Universal Action (default ⌘/) → Upload to ImgBed
• Copy a screenshot (⌘⌃⇧4) or an image → press the Hotkey, or type imgbed
• Test the connection: imgbed-test (uploads a 1×1 PNG)

On success: a notification, the URL on the clipboard, and actions to copy Markdown/HTML, open the image, or open /dashboard.
On failure the clipboard is left unchanged. The auth code is not exported with the .alfredworkflow.</string>
